# Juggle Counter (JuggleJs)

Web app that counts **football juggles** from a live webcam or a test video file. Inspired by [JuggleNet](https://github.com/Logan1904/JuggleNet.git). PoC: https://andruwik777.github.io/JuggleJs

## Architecture

- **Single Page Application** — one HTML page per entry point (`index.html` live webcam, `test-juggle-video.html` video test). No router, no backend.
- **Vanilla JS** — no React, Vue, bundler, or build step. All logic in `js/app.js` (ES module).
- **Simple styles, simple JS** — CSS in each HTML `<style>` block; direct DOM create/reuse, no virtual DOM.
- **Aimed for mobile devices** — focused primarily on Android and iOS mobile devices (portrait orientation).

## Key files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.html` | Live webcam UI, fullscreen session, voice-count toggle |
| `test-juggle-video.html` | Video regression test; wraps `window.runJuggleTest()` |
| `js/app.js` | Detection, counting, Kalman, visualization, voice, test API |
| `models/model_fp16.tflite` | Custom MediaPipe object-detection model (juggling ball) |

## How juggle counting works

1. **MediaPipe ObjectDetector** detects the ball bounding box each frame.
2. **1D Kalman filters** (X/Y, JuggleNet model) smooth position; predict when detection is missing (`calculatedOnly`).
3. **Peak detection** (`isNewJuggleDetected`): local Y maximum with amplitude ≥ half ball diameter = one juggle.
4. **`ballState`** ring buffer for trajectory and debug viz (`STATE_BUFFER_CAPACITY ≈ window width / 5`).
5. Optional **Web Speech API** voice count ("One", "Two", …) via `#voiceCountCheckbox`.

## Debug capabilities (preserve when changing code)

1. **Ball overlay** — MediaPipe bbox (`.highlighter`) with camera-pixel label; Extended colors match snake dots and shows Kalman center.
2. **Position timeline** — snake plot: OFF / Simple / Extended; blue/cycle detect, red Kalman-only, yellow minY, green juggle; Extended adds right-side debug table in camera pixels.
3. **Timing stats** — AI ms, PostAI ms, total ms / FPS, plus `videoWidth×videoHeight`.
4. **Video test DEBUG mode** — frame-by-frame seek + `runOneDetectionFrame()` for DevTools breakpoints; realtime mode uses `video.play()`.

Keep debug overlays working; do not hide diagnostics behind flags unless requested.

## Test API

- `window.runJuggleTest(videoUrl)` → `{ start(debugMode), result: Promise<number> }`
- Events: `juggleAppReady`, `juggleTestReadyToRun`
- User gesture required before video/audio (browser autoplay policy)
